package validations

import (
	"kena.bot/api-db-go/internal/domain/dbguild"
)

// UpdateModuleModerationBody mirrors the Node `updateModuleModerationSchema`
// (a `.strict()` object of `.optional()` fields). The handler decodes this
// with `DisallowUnknownFields` (matching the zod `.strict()` — unknown
// keys top-level OR nested are a 400) and then re-decodes the SAME raw
// body as `map[string]any`, which the repository merges into the existing
// subdoc via `mongo.MergeDeepJSON` by KEY PRESENCE: a key absent in the
// body is left alone; an explicit `false`/`0`/`""`/`null` is applied and
// overrides the stored value; nested objects (`commands_global`, `mute`,
// `automod`) recurse; the `commands` map merges per-key; slices replace
// wholesale.
//
// UNLIKE the READ schema, the PATCH schema exposes NO `schema_version`
// / `updated_at` — those are stamped by the repo on every write. Every
// other READ field IS patchable here (the READ and PATCH catalogs
// otherwise match).
//
// `log_channel_id` is the only TOP-LEVEL nullable string (`string |
// null`). Because merge is presence-based, sending `null` clears it to
// null and omitting the key preserves the stored value — exactly like
// Node's `mergeDeep`, with no special-case handling in this struct. The
// nested nullables (`mute.role_id`, each command's `dm_embed.color`)
// ride inside their parent structs and are merged recursively.
//
// REMAINING CAVEATS (inherited from the old MergeDeep mold, NOT from
// presence-based behaviour):
//   - Go's json decoder does NOT enforce zod's REQUIRED-ness inside a
//     present nested object (Node's `commandAccessUpdateSchema` /
//     `automod*` rule schemas are `.strict()` with every field
//     required), so a partial nested object that Node would 400 is
//     accepted here and the missing leaves stay zero — the same
//     non-strict-required behaviour every Go module body has.
//   - The zod value constraints (`dm_embed.content` max 4000) are NOT
//     enforced here. Same as every other Go module body.
//
// Cada clave de nivel superior del schema DEBE tener su puntero aquí: si falta
// una, el PATCH de la dashboard se come un 400 "unknown field" (el handler
// decodifica con `DisallowUnknownFields`). Por eso los siete bloques del v3
// (`protection`, `escalation`, `effects`, `raid`, `gate`, `antinuke`,
// `lockdown`) están listados igual que `automod` — y `flows` (v4) igual.
//
// `Flows` reutiliza `dbguild.ModerationFlow` TAL CUAL (mismo precedente que
// `Creators *[]dbguild.TempvoiceCreator` / `TicketTypes *[]dbguild.TicketsType`
// / `TicketTypes *[]dbguild.ModmailTicketType`), no un tipo "Body" duplicado:
// el struct de dominio YA tiene exactamente la forma que la dashboard envía
// (§5.3 del contrato de flujos: el PATCH sustituye el array ENTERO, así que
// cada flujo llega completo, con `id`/`created_at`/`updated_at` incluidos).
// Los `params` de trigger/condiciones/pasos siguen siendo `map[string]any`
// libre — su forma la valida el catálogo compartido, no Go — así que
// `DisallowUnknownFields` no los toca; sí rechaza cualquier clave desconocida
// a nivel de `ModerationFlow`/`ModerationFlowScope`/etc., que es justo lo que
// se quiere.
type UpdateModuleModerationBody struct {
	Enabled            *bool                                 `json:"enabled,omitempty"`
	CommandMode        *dbguild.ModerationCommandMode        `json:"command_mode,omitempty"`
	CommandsGlobal     *dbguild.ModerationCommandAccess      `json:"commands_global,omitempty"`
	Commands           *map[string]dbguild.ModerationCommand `json:"commands,omitempty"`
	Mute               *dbguild.ModerationMute               `json:"mute,omitempty"`
	LogChannelID       *string                               `json:"log_channel_id,omitempty"`
	TrackNativeActions *bool                                 `json:"track_native_actions,omitempty"`
	Automod            *dbguild.ModerationAutomod            `json:"automod,omitempty"`
	Protection         *dbguild.ModerationProtection         `json:"protection,omitempty"`
	Escalation         *dbguild.ModerationEscalation         `json:"escalation,omitempty"`
	Effects            *dbguild.ModerationEffects            `json:"effects,omitempty"`
	Raid               *dbguild.ModerationRaid               `json:"raid,omitempty"`
	Gate               *dbguild.ModerationGate               `json:"gate,omitempty"`
	Antinuke           *dbguild.ModerationAntinuke           `json:"antinuke,omitempty"`
	Lockdown           *dbguild.ModerationLockdown           `json:"lockdown,omitempty"`
	Flows              *[]dbguild.ModerationFlow             `json:"flows,omitempty"`
}
